IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-interpretation`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026
-- (a rendering, not the official text). Part 5 Division 2: s 148 (an undischarged bankrupt), s 149 (disqualification of unfit
-- directors of insolvent companies), s 149A (companies wound up on grounds of national security or interest).
--
-- The Court, the Minister, the Official Receiver, the Official Assignee and the liquidator appear only as what they mean to the
-- individual (what may be done to the person, what the person may do, what follows). Judgments the text hands to the Court
-- (unfit, satisfied, thinks fit) are plain inputs named for the fact. JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no; NOTHING the text does not say.
-- A bar is named as a bar: JUST TRUE means "the section bars it".

§ `Section 148: an undischarged bankrupt`

DECLARE `s 148(1) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1) the offence of an undischarged bankrupt who acts as director of, or takes part in the management of, any corporation, except with permission.
-- s 4(7) widens "undischarged bankrupt" to an insolvent under any written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency: the keel answers it.
-- src:11925 | 148.—(1) Every person who, being an undischarged bankrupt
-- src:11926 | (whether the person was adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a
-- src:11927 | foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy), acts as director of, or
-- src:11928 | directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management
-- src:11929 | of, any corporation, except with the permission of the Court or the
-- src:11930 | written permission of the Official Assignee, shall be guilty of an
-- src:11931 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:11932 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:11933 | both.
@ref s 148(1) (src:11925-11933)
GIVEN `the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the permission of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    (`the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy`
           OR `s 4(7) a reference to a person being an undischarged bankrupt covers the person being an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent` FALSE `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
      AND `the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation`
      AND (NOT `the person has the permission of the Court`)
      AND (NOT `the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Every person who, being an undischarged bankrupt ..., acts as director of, or ... takes part in or is concerned in the management of, any corporation, except with the permission of the Court or the written permission of the Official Assignee, shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet or the "except" is met

@ref s 148(1) (src:11925-11933)
GIVEN `the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the permission of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 148(1) penalty`
`s 148(1) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 148(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is an undischarged bankrupt, whether adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy` `the person is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` `the person acts as director of, or directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management of, a corporation` `the person has the permission of the Court` `the person has the written permission of the Official Assignee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 148(1) penalty` OF 10000, 2 TIMES 12, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (written 2 TIMES 12 months) or both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (2) on the application, the Court or the Official Assignee may refuse it or approve it subject to conditions.
-- src:11939 | (2) On an application by an undischarged bankrupt under
-- src:11940 | subsection (1) to the Court or the Official Assignee (as the case
-- src:11941 | may be) the Court or the Official Assignee may refuse the application
-- src:11942 | or approve the application subject to such condition as the Court or
-- src:11943 | the Official Assignee (as the case may be) may impose.
@ref s 148(2) (src:11939-11943)
GIVEN `the application is by an undischarged bankrupt under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(2) the Court or the Official Assignee may refuse the application or approve it subject to conditions` MEANS
    IF `the application is by an undischarged bankrupt under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On an application by an undischarged bankrupt under subsection (1) ... the Court or the Official Assignee may refuse the application or approve" -- an "on application" gate that fails (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), "upon" counted as "where" by ruling (c) of the same date); a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

-- (3) the Court must not give permission unless notice has been served on the Minister and the Official Assignee, who may be represented and oppose.
-- src:11945 | (3) The Court must not give permission under this section unless
-- src:11946 | notice of intention to apply therefor has been served on the Minister
-- src:11947 | and on the Official Assignee and the Minister and the Official
-- src:11948 | Assignee or either of them may be represented at the hearing of and
-- src:11949 | may oppose the granting of the application.
@ref s 148(3) (src:11945-11949)
GIVEN `notice of intention to apply has been served on the Minister and on the Official Assignee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister and the Official Assignee, or either of them, may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(3) the subsection bars the Court from giving permission` MEANS
    IF `notice of intention to apply has been served on the Minister and on the Official Assignee` AND `the Minister and the Official Assignee, or either of them, may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court must not give permission under this section unless notice of intention to apply therefor has been served on the Minister and on the Official Assignee and the Minister and the Official Assignee or either of them may be represented" -- the "unless" is met
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4) a person granted permission must lodge a copy with the Registrar within 14 days after the order or written permission issues.
-- src:11953 | (4) Any person who has been granted permission by the Court or
-- src:11954 | written permission by the Official Assignee under subsection (1)
-- src:11955 | must, within 14 days after the issue of the Court order or written
-- src:11956 | permission, lodge a copy of the order or written permission with the
-- src:11957 | Registrar.
@ref s 148(4) (src:11953-11957)
GIVEN `the date the Court order or written permission was issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 148(4) the last day for lodging the copy of the order or written permission` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the Court order or written permission was issued` 14 Days

@ref s 148(4) (src:11953-11957)
GIVEN `the person has been granted permission by the Court or written permission by the Official Assignee under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the Court order or written permission was issued` IS A DATE
      `the date the copy was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(4) the person has lodged the copy within the time the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the person has been granted permission by the Court or written permission by the Official Assignee under subsection (1)`
    THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the Court order or written permission was issued` `the date the copy was lodged with the Registrar` 14 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 14 days after the issue of the Court order or written permission, lodge a copy" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)); "within N days after" is read as "not later than the last day" (fork line in NOTES.md)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who has been granted permission" -- a scope limit with no "only"

§ `Regulative rules: section 148(1) and (4)`

DECLARE `s 148 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 148(1) act as director of, or take part in the management of, a corporation without the permission of the Court or the written permission of the Official Assignee`
    `s 148(4) lodge a copy of the Court order or written permission with the Registrar`

-- (1): the prohibition derived from the offence (N2 of 2026-11-04: the bearer, an undischarged bankrupt, is named).
-- src:11925 | 148.—(1) Every person who, being an undischarged bankrupt
-- src:11926 | (whether the person was adjudged bankrupt by a Singapore Court or a
-- src:11927 | foreign court having jurisdiction in bankruptcy), acts as director of, or
-- src:11928 | directly or indirectly takes part in or is concerned in the management
-- src:11929 | of, any corporation, except with the permission of the Court or the
-- src:11930 | written permission of the Official Assignee, shall be guilty of an
-- src:11931 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:11932 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:11933 | both.
@ref s 148(1) (src:11925-11933)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 148 act`
`s 148(1) an undischarged bankrupt must not act as director without permission` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 148(1) act as director of, or take part in the management of, a corporation without the permission of the Court or the written permission of the Official Assignee`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "an undischarged bankrupt acted as director of, or took part in the management of, a corporation without permission"

-- (4): the lodging within 14 days. The clock counts days from the issue of the order or written permission.
-- src:11953 | (4) Any person who has been granted permission by the Court or
-- src:11954 | written permission by the Official Assignee under subsection (1)
-- src:11955 | must, within 14 days after the issue of the Court order or written
-- src:11956 | permission, lodge a copy of the order or written permission with the
-- src:11957 | Registrar.
@ref s 148(4) (src:11953-11957)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 148 act`
`s 148(4) a person granted permission must lodge a copy within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MUST `s 148(4) lodge a copy of the Court order or written permission with the Registrar`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the copy of the Court order or written permission was not lodged with the Registrar within 14 days after its issue"

§ `Section 149: disqualification of unfit directors of insolvent companies`

DECLARE `s 149(12) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (5)(a): the date on which a company has gone into liquidation, by which of the three routes.
DECLARE `s 149(5)(a) how the company went into liquidation` IS ONE OF
    `s 149(5)(a)(i) it was wound up by the Court`
    `s 149(5)(a)(ii) a provisional liquidator was appointed under section 161(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 149(5)(a)(iii) any other case`

-- src:12037 | (5) For the purposes of this section —
-- src:12039 | (a) a company has gone into liquidation —
-- src:12041 | (i) if it is wound up by the Court, on the date of the filing
-- src:12042 | of the winding up application;
-- src:12044 | (ii) where a provisional liquidator was appointed under
-- src:12045 | section 161(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:12046 | Dissolution Act 2018, at the time when the
-- src:12047 | declaration made under that subsection was lodged
-- src:12048 | with the Registrar; and
-- src:12050 | (iii) in any other case, on the date of the passing of the
-- src:12051 | resolution for the voluntary winding up; and
@ref s 149(5)(a) (src:12037-12051)
GIVEN `how the company went into liquidation` IS A `s 149(5)(a) how the company went into liquidation`
      `the date of the filing of the winding up application` IS A DATE
      `the date the declaration made under section 161(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the date of the passing of the resolution for the voluntary winding up` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 149(5)(a) the date on which the company has gone into liquidation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the company went into liquidation`
    WHEN `s 149(5)(a)(i) it was wound up by the Court` THEN `the date of the filing of the winding up application`
    WHEN `s 149(5)(a)(ii) a provisional liquidator was appointed under section 161(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` THEN `the date the declaration made under section 161(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 was lodged with the Registrar`
    WHEN `s 149(5)(a)(iii) any other case` THEN `the date of the passing of the resolution for the voluntary winding up`

-- (5)(b): the company was insolvent at the time it went into liquidation if it was unable to pay its debts within section 125(2) of the 2018 Act.
-- src:12053 | (b) a company was insolvent at the time it has gone into
-- src:12054 | liquidation if it was unable to pay its debts, within the
-- src:12055 | meaning of that expression in section 125(2) of the
-- src:12056 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018,
@ref s 149(5)(b) (src:12053-12056)
GIVEN `the company was unable to pay its debts, within the meaning of section 125(2) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(5)(b) the company was insolvent at the time it went into liquidation` MEANS
    IF `the company was unable to pay its debts, within the meaning of section 125(2) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company was insolvent at the time it has gone into liquidation if it was unable to pay its debts, within the meaning of that expression in section 125(2)" -- a condition introduced with "if" that fails

-- (5), closing words: references in the section to a person's conduct as a director include, where the company has become insolvent, conduct in relation to any matter connected with or arising out of the insolvency.
-- src:12061 | and references in this section to a person’s conduct as a director of any
-- src:12062 | company or companies include, where any of those companies have
-- src:12063 | become insolvent, references to that person’s conduct in relation to
-- src:12064 | any matter connected with or arising out of the insolvency of that
-- src:12065 | company.
@ref s 149(5) (src:12061-12065)
GIVEN `the company has become insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is conduct in relation to a matter connected with or arising out of the insolvency of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(5) the person's conduct as a director of the company includes the conduct in relation to a matter connected with the insolvency` MEANS
    IF `the company has become insolvent` AND `the conduct is conduct in relation to a matter connected with or arising out of the insolvency of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references in this section to a person's conduct as a director of any company or companies include, where any of those companies have become insolvent, references to that person's conduct in relation to any matter connected with or arising out of the insolvency of that company" leaves the meaning open

-- (10) the section applies only to a company that has gone into insolvent liquidation on or after 15 August 1984.
-- src:12149 | (10) This section does not apply unless the company mentioned in
-- src:12150 | subsection (2)(b) has gone into insolvent liquidation on or after
-- src:12151 | 15 August 1984 and the conduct to which the Court is to have regard
-- src:12152 | does not include conduct as a director of a company that has gone into
-- src:12153 | liquidation before that date.
@ref s 149(10) (src:12149-12153)
GIVEN `the date the company went into insolvent liquidation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(10) the section applies to the company's liquidation` MEANS
    IF `the date the company went into insolvent liquidation` AT LEAST Date 15 8 1984
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply unless the company mentioned in subsection (2)(b) has gone into insolvent liquidation on or after 15 August 1984" -- the "unless" is not met

@ref s 149(10) (src:12150-12153)
GIVEN `the date the company that the person's conduct as a director concerned went into liquidation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(10) the conduct as a director of the company is conduct to which the Court is to have regard` MEANS
    IF `the date the company that the person's conduct as a director concerned went into liquidation` LESS THAN Date 15 8 1984
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the conduct to which the Court is to have regard does not include conduct as a director of a company that has gone into liquidation before that date"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection excludes conduct in a company that went into liquidation before 15 August 1984 and does not say what counts

-- (2)(b)(i): the person is or has been a director of a company that has at any time gone into liquidation (while a director or within 3 years of ceasing) and was insolvent then.
-- src:11988 | (b) in respect of the person —
-- src:11990 | (i) he or she is or has been a director of a company
-- src:11991 | which has at any time gone into liquidation (whether
-- src:11992 | while he or she was a director or within 3 years of his
-- src:11993 | or her ceasing to be a director) and was insolvent at
-- src:11994 | that time; and
@ref s 149(2)(b)(i) (src:11988-11994)
GIVEN `the person is or has been a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is still a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person ceased to be a director of the company` IS A DATE
      `the date the company went into liquidation` IS A DATE
      `the company was insolvent at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(2)(b)(i) the person is or has been a director of a company that went into liquidation and was insolvent at that time` MEANS
    IF    `the person is or has been a director of the company`
      AND (`the person is still a director of the company` OR `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the person ceased to be a director of the company` `the date the company went into liquidation` 3 Years)
      AND `the company was insolvent at that time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in respect of the person -- (i) he or she is or has been a director of a company which has at any time gone into liquidation (whether while he or she was a director or within 3 years of his or her ceasing to be a director) and was insolvent at that time" -- a matter the Court must be satisfied of, unmet

-- (2): the Court must make a disqualification order if satisfied of (a) 14 days' notice and (b)(i), (b)(ii). The date notice was given and the date of hearing are
-- taken as the test of "not less than 14 days' notice of the application" (fork line in NOTES.md).
-- src:11982 | (2) The Court must make a disqualification order under
-- src:11983 | subsection (1) if it is satisfied that —
-- src:11985 | (a) the person against whom the order is sought has been given
-- src:11986 | not less than 14 days’ notice of the application; and
-- src:11988 | (b) in respect of the person —
-- src:11990 | (i) he or she is or has been a director of a company
-- src:11991 | which has at any time gone into liquidation (whether
-- src:11992 | while he or she was a director or within 3 years of his
-- src:11993 | or her ceasing to be a director) and was insolvent at
-- src:11994 | that time; and
-- src:11996 | (ii) his or her conduct as director of that company either
-- src:11997 | taken alone or taken together with his or her conduct
-- src:11998 | as a director of any other company or companies
-- src:11999 | makes him or her unfit to be a director of or in any
-- src:12000 | way, whether directly or indirectly, be concerned in,
-- src:12001 | or take part in, the management of a company.
@ref s 149(2) (src:11982-12001)
GIVEN `the date the person was given notice of the application` IS A DATE
      `the date of the hearing of the application` IS A DATE
      `the person is or has been a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is still a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person ceased to be a director of the company` IS A DATE
      `the date the company went into liquidation` IS A DATE
      `the company was insolvent at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the conduct of the person as director of that company, alone or together with the person's conduct as a director of any other company or companies, makes the person unfit to be concerned in the management of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(2) the Court must make a disqualification order against the person` MEANS
    IF    `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the person was given notice of the application` `the date of the hearing of the application` 14 Days
      AND `s 149(2)(b)(i) the person is or has been a director of a company that went into liquidation and was insolvent at that time` `the person is or has been a director of the company` `the person is still a director of the company` `the date the person ceased to be a director of the company` `the date the company went into liquidation` `the company was insolvent at that time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `the Court is satisfied that the conduct of the person as director of that company, alone or together with the person's conduct as a director of any other company or companies, makes the person unfit to be concerned in the management of a company`
      AND `s 149(10) the section applies to the company's liquidation` `the date the company went into liquidation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court must make a disqualification order under subsection (1) if it is satisfied that -- (a) ...; and (b) ..." -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a), fork line in NOTES.md); with subsection (10): "This section does not apply unless ... on or after 15 August 1984"

-- (1): the Court may make the order on the application of the Minister or the Official Receiver as in (9), on being satisfied as to the matters in (2),
-- for a period not exceeding 5 years after the date of the order.
