      `the Court is satisfied as to the matters referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(1) the Court may make an order disqualifying the person` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by the Minister or the Official Receiver as provided for in subsection (9)` AND `the Court is satisfied as to the matters referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court may -- (a) on the application of the Minister or the Official Receiver as provided for in subsection (9); and (b) on being satisfied as to the matters referred to in subsection (2), make an order" -- an "on" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05 counts "upon" as "where") that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

@ref s 149(1) (src:11976-11980)
GIVEN `the period the order specifies, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(1) the period the order specifies is within the limit the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the period the order specifies, in years` AT MOST 5
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during such period not exceeding 5 years after the date of the order as is specified in the order"

