      `it appears to the Official Receiver, or to the liquidator, that the conditions mentioned in subsection (2)(b) are satisfied as respects the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(3) the Official Receiver or the liquidator must immediately report the matter to the Minister` MEANS
    IF `the person is or has been a director of a company that is being wound up` AND `it appears to the Official Receiver, or to the liquidator, that the conditions mentioned in subsection (2)(b) are satisfied as respects the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If in the case of a person who is or has been a director of the company which is ... being wound up ..., it appears ... that the conditions mentioned in subsection (2)(b) are satisfied ..., the Official Receiver or the liquidator ... must immediately report the matter to the Minister" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a), fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (4) the Court may order the Official Receiver or liquidator to make good a default in complying with the Minister's requirement.
-- src:12020 | (4) The Minister may require the Official Receiver or the liquidator
-- src:12021 | or the former liquidator of a company —
-- src:12023 | (a) to furnish the Minister with such information with respect
-- src:12024 | to any person’s conduct as a director of the company; and
-- src:12026 | (b) to produce and permit inspection of such books, papers and
-- src:12027 | other records relevant to that person’s conduct as such a
-- src:12028 | director,
-- src:12030 | as the Minister may reasonably require for the purpose of determining
-- src:12031 | whether to exercise, or of exercising, any of the Minister’s functions
-- src:12032 | under this section; and if default is made in complying with that
-- src:12033 | requirement the Court may, on the application of the Minister, make
-- src:12034 | an order requiring that person to make good the default within such
-- src:12035 | time as is specified in the order.
@ref s 149(4) (src:12020-12035)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with the Minister's requirement for information or for the production of books, papers and other records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister applies to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(4) the Court may order the person to make good the default` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with the Minister's requirement for information or for the production of books, papers and other records` AND `the Minister applies to the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if default is made in complying with that requirement the Court may, on the application of the Minister, make an order" -- a gate introduced with "if" and "on the application" that fails; a "may" with an "on application" gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

-- (6): the matters the Court must have regard to; (7) the Minister may add to or vary them by notification.
DECLARE `s 149(6) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 149(6)(a)(i) whether there has been any misfeasance or breach of any fiduciary or other duty by the director in relation to the company`
    `s 149(6)(a)(ii) whether there has been any misapplication or retention by the director of, or any conduct giving rise to an obligation to account for, any money or other property of the company`
    `s 149(6)(a)(iii) the extent of the director's responsibility for any failure by the company to comply with sections 138, 190, 191, 196B, 197, 199 and 201`
    `s 149(6)(b)(i) the extent of the director's responsibility for the causes of the company becoming insolvent`
    `s 149(6)(b)(ii) the extent of the director's responsibility for any failure by the company to supply any goods or services which have been paid for (in whole or in part)`
    `s 149(6)(b)(iii) the extent of the director's responsibility for the company entering into any transaction liable to be set aside under section 130(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 149(6)(b)(iv) whether the causes of the company becoming insolvent are attributable to its carrying on business in a particular industry where the risk of insolvency is generally recognised to be higher`
    `s 149(6) some other matter`

-- src:12069 | (6) In deciding whether a person’s conduct as a director of any
