GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(6) the Court must have regard to the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter` EQUALS `s 149(6) some other matter`
    THEN (IF `the Minister has added the matter by notification in the Gazette under subsection (7)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the Court "must in relation to his or her conduct ... have regard, generally to the matters referred to in paragraph (a), and, in particular, to the matters referred to in paragraph (b)"; the text lists them without "only" and says nothing of other matters
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 149(6) (src:12076-12077)
