§ `Section 149A: companies wound up on grounds of national security or interest`

DECLARE `s 149A(4) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1) the Court may, on the Minister's application, disqualify a director of a company ordered wound up under s 125(1)(n) of the 2018 Act
-- for 3 years from the date of the winding up order.
-- src:12193 | 149A.—(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), where a company is
-- src:12194 | ordered to be wound up by the Court under section 125(1)(n) of the
-- src:12195 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 on the ground
-- src:12196 | that it is being used for purposes against national security or interest,
-- src:12197 | the Court may, on the application of the Minister, make an order
-- src:12198 | (called in this section a disqualification order) disqualifying any
-- src:12199 | person who is a director of that company from being a director or in
-- src:12200 | any way, directly or indirectly, being concerned in, or from taking
-- src:12205 | part in, the management of any company or foreign company for a
-- src:12206 | period of 3 years from the date of the making of the winding up order.
@ref s 149A(1) (src:12193-12206)
GIVEN `the company is ordered to be wound up by the Court under section 125(1)(n) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 on the ground that it is being used for purposes against national security or interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister applies to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149A(1) the Court may make an order disqualifying the person` MEANS
    IF    `the company is ordered to be wound up by the Court under section 125(1)(n) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 on the ground that it is being used for purposes against national security or interest`
      AND `the person is a director of that company`
      AND `the Minister applies to the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a company is ordered to be wound up by the Court under section 125(1)(n) ... the Court may, on the application of the Minister, make an order ... disqualifying any person who is a director of that company" -- a "where" gate (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)) that fails; a "may" with a "where" gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

@ref s 149A(1) (src:12205-12206)
GIVEN `the date of the making of the winding up order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 149A(1) the last day of the disqualification` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the making of the winding up order` 3 Years

